From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:55:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pex-stun: without a raw socket, refresh the data port while
 no peer is up

Without a raw socket the data port is measured once, by taking the port over
from WireGuard before any peer connects, and never again: later rounds learn
the auth port and stop. A NAT whose mapping has moved since then is never
noticed, and the host keeps announcing a port nobody can reach.

After each auth port refresh, take the port over again for the data query
when no peer is connected. Nothing flows on the port then, and a peer that
stays down may be down exactly because the announced port is stale. With a
peer up the port is proven to work and the round ends as before. If the
takeover socket cannot be opened, end the round rather than querying the
auth port in a loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019FGFD5nZ9AL3AdMi7SfYSg
---
 pex-stun.c | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pex-stun.c b/pex-stun.c
index 05ceefa..594aa42 100644
--- a/pex-stun.c
+++ b/pex-stun.c
@@ -245,13 +245,22 @@ void network_stun_rx_packet(struct network *net, const void *data, size_t len)
 	/*
 	 * Learning the auth (PEX) port is only the first step towards the
 	 * WireGuard data port, which needs a raw socket to forge its source
-	 * port. Without one (an unprivileged Android app) that second step is
-	 * unreachable, so stop here instead of re-querying forever.
+	 * port. Without one (an unprivileged Android app) the only way to the
+	 * data port is to take it over from WireGuard for a moment, which is
+	 * acceptable while no peer is up (nothing is flowing, and a peer that
+	 * stays down may be down exactly because the port has moved). With a
+	 * peer up the port is known to work; stop instead of re-querying
+	 * forever.
 	 */
-	if (s->req_auth_port && pex_raw_socket(AF_INET) >= 0)
+	if (s->req_auth_port && pex_raw_socket(AF_INET) >= 0) {
 		stun->state = STUN_STATE_STUN_QUERY_SEND;
-	else
+	} else if (s->req_auth_port && !has_connected_peer(net, false)) {
+		network_stun_open_socket(net);
+		stun->state = stun->wgport_disabled ?
+			STUN_STATE_STUN_QUERY_SEND : STUN_STATE_IDLE;
+	} else {
 		stun->state = STUN_STATE_IDLE;
+	}
 
 	network_stun_query_clear_pending(net);
 
